    "title": "Umbrella weather for Thursday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Deitra McKenzie ,\n1 hours ago MERIDIAN, Miss. (WTOK) - An area of low pressure will move across the Northern Gulf on Thursday, and it’ll bring us a likely chance for experiencing bouts of rain throughout the day. The highest rain chances will be both Thursday morning and evening. We’re expecting a little bit of a lull during the afternoon as the rain coverage becomes less & more scattered. Thankfully, severe storms aren’t expected. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
